course: dictionary
lesson: 5851
title: Working out a new word from its context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A Malinois is a type of dog, called a breed. A breed is a particular kind of animal that has been bred to have the same looks and features. Malinois is a name for one breed, so it starts with a capital letter.
explain: Use the context to work out what a word means. «Police forces use dogs, very often German shepherds and Belgian Malinois, to track people.» German shepherds are dogs, and the clues police and track people tell you what these dogs do. So a Malinois must be a kind of dog that helps police.
explain: Ask yourself why the writer says something. The sentence goes on: these breeds are strong, quick to learn and good at following a scent. Those are the reasons police choose them. Finding the reason helps you understand the whole sentence, not just the hard word.
fact: A Malinois is a breed of Belgian Shepherd dog.
fact: It has short fawn fur and a dark face.
fact: Malinois dogs are very clever and full of energy.
fact: They are often trained as police, army or search-and-rescue dogs.
fact: «Owners need lots of time to train and exercise them.»
exercise: «Police forces use dogs, very often German shepherds and Belgian Malinois, to track people.» What kind of animal is a Malinois? | A fish | A bird | *A dog
exercise: «Malinois dogs are strong, quick to learn and good at following a scent.» Why do police choose Malinois dogs? | They have long white fur | *They are quick to learn and good at following a scent | They can talk to people
exercise: Mia says a Malinois must be a type of cat. Which words in «Police forces use dogs, very often German shepherds and Belgian Malinois» prove her wrong? | *the words dogs and German shepherds | the word police | the word very | the word people
test: Mia says a Malinois dog is lazy and sleeps all day. What does the dictionary suggest? | Malinois dogs are a kind of cat | Malinois dogs sleep all day | Malinois dogs have long black fur | *Malinois dogs are very clever and full of energy
test: «Owners need lots of time to train and exercise them.» What does this tell you about Malinois dogs? | They only need one short walk a year | They never need to go outside | They need no training at all | *They need a lot of training and exercise
exam: Using the context, what does Malinois mean? | A helpful word for a shop | A type of bird that sings | *A breed of Belgian Shepherd dog, often trained as a police or search dog | A kind of police car
